  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, homeowners insurance covers a roof leak only if a sudden, accidental event\u2014like a severe windstorm, hail, heavy snow loads, or a fallen tree\u2014causes the damage. It does not cover leaks resulting from normal wear and tear, old age, or a lack of routine maintenance."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The\nUtah Insurance Department\noutlines that standard policies are meant for unexpected losses rather than aging home materials.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Covered vs. Excluded Causes"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Wind and Hail: Severe Wasatch Front or mountain storms that rip off shingles or bruise/fracture materials are usually covered."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Falling Objects:\nTree branches or debris crashing through the roof during a storm are covered."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ice Dams: Heavy winter snow and ice buildup that forces water under shingles and leaks inside is often covered, depending on specific policy limits."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Wear and Tear:\nGradual rotting, loose flashing, or aging shingles left unmaintained are excluded."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Neglect: Failing to clear heavy ice or fix known minor roof damage over time voids the claim."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What caused\nthe roof leak (a recent storm, heavy snow, or old age)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Is there any interior ceiling or wall damage?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you figure out your next steps or what to document for an insurance claim."
      }
    ],
